From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: new full-screen R8 color targets start at 1.0, not stale memory

A render target that reuses memory of earlier ones was uploaded from guest memory, which
holds stale bytes: the GPU-written targets there never went back to guest memory.
Wytchwood (PPSA05721) reads its interaction mask before drawing into it, so the whole
screen turned to noise near objects; starting the mask at 0 drew white outlines instead.
New full-screen R8 color targets with no CPU or buffer writes now start at 1.0.
---
diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/textureCache.cpp b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/textureCache.cpp
index 9f292d57f203a56ff3fe64eed4073b5f44e20c31..db558a5236a4ab66b790b42f85a96fc77f68c643 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/textureCache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/textureCache.cpp
@@ -1025,6 +1025,23 @@ void TextureCache::InitializeImage(ImageId id) {
 		return;
 	}
 	const bool upload = image.IsBufferModified() || image.IsCpuDirty();
+	// EmuFive: a new full-screen R8 color target over guest memory no CPU or buffer write
+	// filled holds bytes left by other render targets, which only ever lived on the host GPU.
+	// Wytchwood (PPSA05721) reads its interaction mask before drawing into it: those bytes
+	// cover the screen in noise, and 0 draws outlines; 1.0 shows the scene as on the console.
+	if (upload && !image.IsBufferModified() && image.IsDefinitelyCpuDirty() &&
+	    image.usage.render_target && !image.depth_id && image.info.samples == 1 &&
+	    image.info.pixel_format == vk::Format::eR8Unorm && image.info.IsTiled() &&
+	    image.info.extent.width >= 1024 && image.info.extent.height >= 512) {
+		image.RefreshComplete();
+		vk::ClearValue full {};
+		full.color.float32[0] = 1.0f;
+		ClearImage(m_scheduler.Current(), id, image.backing.format,
+		           {vk::ImageAspectFlagBits::eColor, 0, image.info.resources.levels, 0,
+		            image.backing.layers},
+		           full);
+		return;
+	}
 	if (upload) {
 		const auto [source, source_offset] =
 		    m_buffer_cache.ObtainBufferForImage(image.info.data.address, image.info.data.size);
